A share that has spent its budget waits on the run queue all the same.
It takes turns before the shares on spare time, and one held to its budget is not;
a share with a ready thread waits on the queue its budget and flags say.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a share waits on another queue than its budget says

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -140,7 +140,7 @@ static struct share **share_queue(const struct share *s)
     if (share_owed(s)) {
         return &run_queue;
     }
-    return (s->flags & SHARE_SPARE) ? &spare_queue : &spent_queue;
+    return &run_queue;
 }
 
 /* Move a share to the queue it now waits on, or take it off the one it was on. */
